# WindyCraft — Infrastructure & DNS Notes

## 1. Domain

**Domain:** `windycraft.com`

The domain is registered and managed through GoDaddy.

GoDaddy is currently being used for DNS management.

---

## 2. Website Hosting

The website is hosted using **GitHub Pages**.

GitHub repository:

`c0lim0n/windycraft`

GitHub Pages URL:

`https://c0lim0n.github.io/windycraft/`

The custom domain configured in GitHub Pages is:

`windycraft.com`

The website is therefore accessed publicly as:

`https://windycraft.com`

The browser remains on `windycraft.com`; it does not visibly redirect to the GitHub Pages URL.

---

## 3. Current DNS Configuration

### Apex / Root Domain

The root domain `windycraft.com` uses four A records pointing to GitHub Pages:

| Type | Host | Value             |
| ---- | ---- | ----------------- |
| A    | @    | `185.199.108.153` |
| A    | @    | `185.199.109.153` |
| A    | @    | `185.199.110.153` |
| A    | @    | `185.199.111.153` |

These are GitHub Pages' documented IP addresses for apex/custom domains.

---

### WWW Subdomain

The `www` hostname uses a CNAME:

| Type  | Host | Value               |
| ----- | ---- | ------------------- |
| CNAME | www  | `c0lim0n.github.io` |

This allows:

`www.windycraft.com`

to resolve to the GitHub Pages site.

---

## 4. Why Four A Records Exist

The four A records are not four servers that I personally manage.

They are GitHub Pages infrastructure addresses provided by GitHub for custom-domain configuration.

All four are configured so that the root domain can correctly reach GitHub Pages.

---

## 5. Website Files

The repository currently contains:

`index.html`

This is the main homepage.

Example structure:

```text
windycraft/
└── index.html
```

Additional documentation files can exist in the repository without affecting the homepage, provided they do not replace or modify `index.html`.

For example:

```text
windycraft/
├── index.html
└── documentation.md
```

The Markdown file does not affect the HTML homepage.

---

## 6. Important DNS Rule

Do not delete the four GitHub Pages A records unless the website is intentionally being moved away from GitHub Pages.

Do not change the `www` CNAME unless the `www` configuration is intentionally being changed.

Other future subdomains can be configured separately.

Example:

`play.windycraft.com`

is independent from:

`windycraft.com`

and can have its own DNS configuration.

---

## 7. Hosting vs Domain

The domain and hosting are separate:

**GoDaddy**
→ Domain registration + DNS management

**GitHub Pages**
→ Website hosting

The domain tells browsers where to find the website, while GitHub Pages provides the actual website files.

